# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Zeros — local environment template
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. These are PUBLIC,
# write-only PostHog *project* keys (the `phc_…` keys), safe to
# ship in the client bundle — they are NOT secret API keys.
#
# Two projects so dev activity never pollutes prod analytics:
#   • VITE_POSTHOG_KEY_DEV  → the "Zeros Dev" PostHog project
#                             (used by `pnpm electron:dev`, ZEROS_DEV=1)
#   • VITE_POSTHOG_KEY_PROD → the "Zeros" PostHog project
#                             (used by the packaged /Applications/Zeros.app)
#
# Leave a key blank to disable analytics for that runtime. With no
# keys at all, analytics is simply off (the app logs an info line).
#
# These are inlined at BUILD time (import.meta.env), so they must be
# present when you run `pnpm dev` / `pnpm build:ui` / package a release.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

VITE_POSTHOG_KEY_DEV=
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY_PROD=

# Optional. Defaults to PostHog US Cloud; override to point at a custom host.
# VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# Optional. Base URL of the web hub (app.zeros.build) the desktop opens for
# sign-in (/launch) and redeems the handoff ticket against (/handoff/redeem).
# Read via import.meta.env.VITE_APP_BASE_URL (renderer) and process.env (main).
# Defaults to https://app.zeros.build — override only for local/preview iteration.
# Non-secret.
# VITE_APP_BASE_URL=https://app.zeros.build

# Feedback → Intercom Worker (apps/feedback-worker). The Help →
# Feedback modal posts here. The URL is public and inlined at BUILD time.
#
# There is no companion token any more. The Worker verifies the user's own
# Auth0 access token and reads the sender's address from its claims. The old
# VITE_FEEDBACK_TOKEN was a shared secret inlined into the renderer bundle —
# readable by anyone holding a build, and since the address was just a body
# field, holding it let you file feedback as any address.
# VITE_FEEDBACK_URL=https://zeros-feedback.<account>.workers.dev

# Release channel for this build: dev | alpha | beta | stable. Drives renderer
# feature-flag gating (apps/desktop/src/renderer/config/release-channel.ts). Usually leave UNSET — unset falls
# back to `import.meta.env.DEV ? "dev" : "stable"`, which is why `pnpm dev` is
# "dev" and release.yml (which does NOT inject this) is "stable". Only the
# alpha and beta workflows set it explicitly, to their own channel.
# Read via import.meta.env.VITE_ZEROS_CHANNEL.
# VITE_ZEROS_CHANNEL=

# ── Internal features (maintainer-only surfaces) ────────────────────────────
# There is NO env var for this. Who can see Settings → Internal is decided by
# `users.staff_role` in the control-plane database, surfaced on GET /v1/me
# (apps/desktop/src/renderer/features/settings/internal-features.ts reads it from the team store).
#
# This used to be VITE_INTERNAL_USER_EMAILS, a build-time allowlist. It was
# removed because Vite inlines VITE_* into the renderer bundle: the addresses
# were readable by anyone who unzipped app.asar out of a published build, so it
# hid nothing while putting real emails into every shipped .app. Grant staff
# with SQL instead — see apps/control-plane/migrations/0007_staff_role.sql.

# ── Auth (Auth0) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mandatory login, but the desktop app never talks to Auth0 directly — ALL
# OAuth happens on app.zeros.build/auth.zeros.build, and the desktop only ever
# exchanges an opaque handoff ticket for a session (apps/desktop/electron/ipc/commands/
# auth-session.ts). So there is no renderer-side Auth0 config at all — nothing
# to set here. VITE_APP_BASE_URL below overrides which deployment the handoff
# talks to.

# ── Control plane (organizations and teams on Railway) ───
# The Organization settings area talks to this service. Unset → that
# area shows a "not configured" state; everything else works normally.
# Read via import.meta.env.VITE_CONTROL_PLANE_URL in the renderer and baked
# into Electron main during `pnpm electron:compile` for GitHub App OAuth.
# VITE_CONTROL_PLANE_URL=https://<your-railway-domain>
